`tests/usage-cli.mjs` changed the child environment only. It filters `PATH` but inherits `ACS_LOGIN_PATH_DIRS`. I verified that agy lookup still includes directories from that variable with an empty `PATH`. If one yields a Gemini seat, the existing Codex registration assertion can pass with that seat alone because it checks `seats.length >= 1`. [tests/usage-cli.mjs:22](/Users/cortega/Documents/Projects/personal/agent-config-studio-wt/agent-config-studio-gemini-usage/tests/usage-cli.mjs:22) · [tests/usage-cli.mjs:62](/Users/cortega/Documents/Projects/personal/agent-config-studio-wt/agent-config-studio-gemini-usage/tests/usage-cli.mjs:62) · [lib/login-path.js:76](/Users/cortega/Documents/Projects/personal/agent-config-studio-wt/agent-config-studio-gemini-usage/lib/login-path.js:76) · [lib/harness.js:693](/Users/cortega/Documents/Projects/personal/agent-config-studio-wt/agent-config-studio-gemini-usage/lib/harness.js:693)

